{"question_text": {"৪৯তম বিসিএস ⎯ ফলিত গণিত (৫৬১)": [{"id": "1", "question": "১) &nbsp;Which of the following is a&nbsp;single-valued function in complex analysis?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_UQPgbxE.png\" width=\"267\" height=\"76\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_X4PJFE3.png\" width=\"263\" height=\"69\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_UqLnxCN.png\" width=\"243\" height=\"59\">", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_olwBKZE.png\" width=\"238\" height=\"60\">", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip4_UajzxAg.png\" width=\"630\" height=\"63\"></p>\r\n<p> </p>"}, {"id": "2", "question": "২) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_1xuA9cY.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"300\" height=\"113\">", "option1": "Exists and equals 1", "option2": "Exists and equals 0", "option3": "Exists and equals <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">i</span></span>", "option4": "Does not exist", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_HJmEN0x.png\" width=\"370\" height=\"112\"></p>"}, {"id": "3", "question": "৩) Which is a necessary and sufficient condition for a function f(z)&nbsp;to be analytic in a region?", "option1": "It is differentiable at one point", "option2": "It satisfies Cauchy–Riemann equations at every point of the region", "option3": "It satisfies CR equations and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">u,v</span></span>&nbsp;have continuous partial derivatives in the region", "option4": "It is bounded in the region", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p>CR equations + continuity of partial derivatives in a neighborhood are the necessary and sufficient conditions for analyticity.</p>"}, {"id": "4", "question": "৪) Let f(z) = e<sup>z</sup>. Which of the following is true?", "option1": "Not analytic anywhere", "option2": "Analytic only on real axis", "option3": "Analytic everywhere", "option4": "Analytic only for&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">Re(z) &gt; 0</span></span>", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_ZQXf4AC.png\" width=\"490\" height=\"211\"></p>"}, {"id": "5", "question": "৫) Which of the following is a <strong data-start=\"158\" data-end=\"183\">Möbius transformation</strong>?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_kcOYcYq.png\" width=\"297\" height=\"63\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_3kjrOqH.png\" width=\"284\" height=\"86\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_v0MXNLs.png\" width=\"298\" height=\"111\">", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_izL1UeD.png\" width=\"273\" height=\"79\">", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip4_108Bd9L.png\" width=\"443\" height=\"31\"></p>"}, {"id": "6", "question": "৬) Which property is always true for Möbius transformations?", "option1": "Maps circles and lines to circles or lines", "option2": "Maps only circles to circles", "option3": "Preserves distance", "option4": "Maps analytic functions to harmonic functions", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p>Möbius transformations are conformal and map circles/lines to circles/lines; they do not necessarily preserve distance.</p>"}, {"id": "7", "question": "৭) The principal value of a multi-valued function is:", "option1": "The average of all possible values", "option2": "One specific branch chosen to make the function single-valued", "option3": "The limit of the function as <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">z→0</span></span>", "option4": "The sum of all possible values", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_rxgl1iy.png\" width=\"487\" height=\"112\"></p>"}, {"id": "8", "question": "৮) Which of the following is a Laurent series?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_OSRVyLF.png\" width=\"318\" height=\"65\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_Hl1xg8K.png\" width=\"292\" height=\"53\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_c1nboiG.png\" width=\"295\" height=\"85\">", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_29qqBKV.png\" width=\"203\" height=\"72\">", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip4_hQhiE3c.png\" width=\"479\" height=\"194\"></p>"}, {"id": "9", "question": "৯) Which of the following complex functions is continuous at every point of the complex plane?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_ueuzfnE.png\" width=\"194\" height=\"102\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_5qn30z1.png\" width=\"182\" height=\"54\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_pLiyODL.png\" width=\"183\" height=\"49\">", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip4_Qvy23H4.png\" width=\"218\" height=\"79\">", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip5_033wllI.png\" width=\"608\" height=\"169\"></p>"}, {"id": "10", "question": "১০) Which of the following functions is&nbsp;harmonic?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_DLwX1IY.png\" width=\"384\" height=\"65\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_GdOdvP4.png\" width=\"352\" height=\"58\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_1w5hW18.png\" width=\"321\" height=\"56\">", "option4": "None", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_zvwFNY4.png\" width=\"484\" height=\"134\"></p>"}, {"id": "11", "question": "১১) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_LQf2ln1.png\" width=\"1045\" height=\"48\">", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_YqqIYyk.png\" width=\"299\" height=\"58\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_0kv4UWP.png\" width=\"292\" height=\"43\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_Bx86eei.png\" width=\"294\" height=\"49\">", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip4_squ5OeD.png\" width=\"338\" height=\"54\">", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>These are the Cauchy–Riemann equations, the necessary conditions for differentiability of a complex function.</p>"}, {"id": "12", "question": "১২) Which of the following functions is differentiable everywhere in <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">C</span></span>?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_21EKmlB.png\" width=\"243\" height=\"79\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_ADMRIrs.png\" width=\"195\" height=\"56\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_jiAnRGo.png\" width=\"202\" height=\"56\">", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_4V1fcGK.png\" width=\"197\" height=\"50\">", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip4_Qdg09QY.png\" width=\"817\" height=\"212\"></p>"}, {"id": "13", "question": "১৩) Which of the following statements is <strong data-start=\"2729\" data-end=\"2737\">true</strong>?", "option1": "Every continuous complex function is differentiable", "option2": "Every differentiable complex function is continuous", "option3": "If limit exists along one path, it exists everywhere", "option4": "All real-valued functions of complex variables are differentiable", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_gDf9GwB.png\" width=\"461\" height=\"180\"></p>"}, {"id": "14", "question": "১৪) Which of the following statements about the limit of a complex function is true?", "option1": "The limit along one path guarantees the general limit exists", "option2": "A limit exists only if the function is differentiable", "option3": "A limit exists if the function approaches the same value from all directions", "option4": "Limits are not defined in complex analysis", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_9ONc2Nq.png\" width=\"507\" height=\"136\"></p>"}, {"id": "15", "question": "১৫) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_y93KlpM.png\" width=\"653\" height=\"96\">", "option1": "Yes, limit = 0", "option2": "Yes, limit = 1", "option3": "No, limit does not exist", "option4": "Yes, limit = ∞", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_X84yMpD.png\" width=\"391\" height=\"270\"></p>"}, {"id": "16", "question": "১৬) The function f(z) = z<sup>1/n </sup>(where n &gt; 1) is:", "option1": "Always single-valued", "option2": "Multi-valued with infinitely many values", "option3": "Multi-valued with exactly <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">n</span></span>&nbsp;distinct values", "option4": "Not a valid complex function", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_2a9gYAr.png\" width=\"563\" height=\"149\"></p>"}, {"id": "17", "question": "১৭) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_J4HSPkm.png\" width=\"732\" height=\"56\">", "option1": "1 + i", "option2": "1 - i", "option3": "1", "option4": "- 1", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_F29Ahai.png\" width=\"422\" height=\"66\"></p>"}, {"id": "18", "question": "১৮) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_BPi3hbX.png\" width=\"473\" height=\"70\">", "option1": "Differentiable everywhere", "option2": "Differentiable only at&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">z = 0</span></span>", "option3": "Not differentiable anywhere", "option4": "Analytic everywhere", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_cse9UzX.png\" width=\"571\" height=\"437\"></p>"}, {"id": "19", "question": "১৯) The real part of an analytic function <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">f(z) = u + iv</span></span>&nbsp;is:", "option1": "Always zero", "option2": "Harmonic", "option3": "Constant", "option4": "Non-differentiable", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_xoQt1nd.png\" width=\"575\" height=\"219\"></p>"}, {"id": "20", "question": "২০) The function <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">f(z) = ∣z∣</span></span>&nbsp;is:", "option1": "Differentiable everywhere", "option2": "Differentiable only at <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">z = 0</span></span>", "option3": "Not differentiable anywhere", "option4": "Analytic everywhere", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_u7OEKAm.png\" width=\"831\" height=\"198\"></p>"}, {"id": "21", "question": "২১) If <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">f(z) = u(x, y) + iv(x, y)</span></span>&nbsp;satisfies CR equations everywhere but <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">u,v</span></span>&nbsp;do <strong data-start=\"2035\" data-end=\"2042\">not</strong> have continuous partial derivatives, then:", "option1": "<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f</span></span></span></span> is analytic", "option2": "<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f</span></span></span></span> may fail to be analytic", "option3": "<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f</span></span></span></span> is entire", "option4": "<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">f</span></span></span></span> is harmonic", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>CR equations alone are necessary but not sufficient. Without continuity of partials in a neighborhood, differentiability may fail ⇒ function may not be analytic.</p>"}, {"id": "22", "question": "২২) Which Möbius transformation maps <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">z = ∞</span></span>?", "option1": "f(z) = 1/z", "option2": "f(z) = z + 1", "option3": "f(z) = 2z", "option4": "f(z) = z<sup>2</sup>", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p>As z→∞z , 1/z→0.</p>"}, {"id": "23", "question": "২৩) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_dRj6mi5.png\" width=\"682\" height=\"57\">", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_6DWmaJO.png\" width=\"210\" height=\"93\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_yGsbqdU.png\" width=\"219\" height=\"59\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_j6K0l9x.png\" width=\"210\" height=\"70\">", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip4_OxDecay.png\" width=\"305\" height=\"73\">", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>This is the standard Taylor series for sin⁡z, convergent for all z.</p>"}, {"id": "24", "question": "২৪) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_8pk5CPv.png\" width=\"854\" height=\"69\">", "option1": "<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">z </span><span class=\"mrel\">= </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span> to 0, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">z = −1</span></span> to ∞", "option2": "<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">z </span><span class=\"mrel\">= -</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span> to 0, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">z = 1</span></span> to ∞&nbsp;", "option3": "<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">z </span><span class=\"mrel\">= </span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span> to 1, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">z = −1</span></span> to -1", "option4": "<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">z </span><span class=\"mrel\">= ∞</span></span></span></span>&nbsp;to 0, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">z = 0</span></span> to ∞", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_S7v1OEy.png\" width=\"422\" height=\"26\"></p>"}, {"id": "25", "question": "২৫) Which function is harmonic&nbsp;<strong data-start=\"1771\" data-end=\"1809\">only along certain lines or curves</strong>?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_D7eHVn0.png\" width=\"335\" height=\"57\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_1PkLC67.png\" width=\"295\" height=\"66\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_GXUxVbK.png\" width=\"303\" height=\"47\">", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_xByGdrM.png\" width=\"293\" height=\"51\">", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip4_rZ09Ua0.png\" width=\"636\" height=\"168\"></p>"}, {"id": "26", "question": "২৬) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_JO78FGg.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"614\" height=\"72\">", "option1": "Itself", "option2": "Imaginary axis", "option3": "Unit circle", "option4": "Infinity", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_2zyuAEo.png\" width=\"437\" height=\"128\"></p>"}, {"id": "27", "question": "২৭) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_KoPu3Ye.png\" width=\"754\" height=\"104\">", "option1": "<span class=\"katex-mathml\">sinh ⁡z</span>", "option2": "<span class=\"mop\">cos</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">z</span>", "option3": "<span class=\"mop\">sin</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">z</span>", "option4": "<span class=\"katex-mathml\">e<sup>z</sup></span>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>Standard Taylor expansion of cosine.</p>"}, {"id": "28", "question": "২৮) Which function has a Laurent series but no Taylor series expansion at z = 0?", "option1": "<span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><sup><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\"><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">z</span></span></span></span></span></span></sup>", "option2": "<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">sin⁡z</span></span>", "option3": "1/z", "option4": "z<sup>2 </sup>+ 1", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_pV0uo4K.png\" width=\"775\" height=\"288\"></p>"}, {"id": "29", "question": "২৯) Which of the following functions is multi-valued?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_NYBi5S7.png\" width=\"240\" height=\"77\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_fMX2aLp.png\" width=\"226\" height=\"63\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_H9f1ki9.png\" width=\"244\" height=\"63\">", "option4": "All of These", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip4_YT8JT0i.png\" width=\"250\" height=\"23\"><br><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip5_LyZEfxS.png\" width=\"498\" height=\"28\"></p>"}, {"id": "30", "question": "৩০) The function&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">f(z)=arg⁡(z)</span></span>&nbsp;is:", "option1": "Single-valued", "option2": "Multi-valued", "option3": "Analytic", "option4": "Entire", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>Argument <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">arg⁡(z)</span></span> can differ by <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">2πk</span></span>. Hence it is multi-valued.</p>"}, {"id": "31", "question": "৩১) The Laurent series differs from the Taylor series because it:", "option1": "Has only positive powers", "option2": "Has both positive and negative powers", "option3": "Does not converge anywhere", "option4": "Is valid only on real axis", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_IPWZnEv.png\" width=\"605\" height=\"275\">Laurent series generalizes Taylor series by allowing negative powers, useful for singularities.</p>"}, {"id": "32", "question": "৩২) Which of the following statements is <strong data-start=\"799\" data-end=\"831\">true for a harmonic function</strong>?", "option1": "It can attain its maximum inside the domain.", "option2": "It satisfies Laplace’s equation.", "option3": "Its derivatives are always zero.", "option4": "It cannot have an imaginary part.", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>By definition, a harmonic function satisfies ∇<sup>2</sup>u=0. Maximum and minimum occur on boundaries (unless constant). Imaginary part is irrelevant for real harmonic functions. </p>"}, {"id": "33", "question": "৩৩) Which of the following is not<strong data-start=\"1332\" data-end=\"1348\">&nbsp;harmonic</strong>?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_YGJF0lm.png\" width=\"275\" height=\"49\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_W8YS7je.png\" width=\"275\" height=\"45\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_eEarlSc.png\" width=\"275\" height=\"53\">", "option4": "All are Harmonic", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p>All three satisfy Laplace Equation. So All of these are Harmonic</p>"}, {"id": "34", "question": "৩৪) Which of the following statements is <strong data-start=\"2281\" data-end=\"2289\">true</strong>?", "option1": "Analyticity at a point implies differentiability in a neighborhood", "option2": "Differentiability at a point implies analyticity in a neighborhood", "option3": "Satisfaction of CR equations at a point is sufficient for analyticity", "option4": "Continuity of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">f</span></span>&nbsp;is sufficient for analyticity", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p>Analyticity requires differentiability in a neighborhood.<br>Differentiability at a single point is not enough.<br>CR equations at a point without continuity do not guarantee analyticity</p>"}, {"id": "35", "question": "৩৫) The function f(z) = (z - 1)<sup>1/2</sup> has how many values?", "option1": "1", "option2": "2", "option3": "Infinitely many", "option4": "None", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_fvT7AK2.png\" width=\"441\" height=\"50\"></p>"}, {"id": "36", "question": "৩৬) Which of the following functions is <strong data-start=\"131\" data-end=\"143\">harmonic</strong> in <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">R<sup>2</sup>∖{0}</span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mclose\">}</span></span></span></span>?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_8rdNv5k.png\" width=\"286\" height=\"48\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_26rIlxQ.png\" width=\"280\" height=\"40\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_FXReVDe.png\" width=\"259\" height=\"51\">", "option4": "All of these", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_tSgx9Vq.png\" width=\"799\" height=\"221\"></p>"}, {"id": "37", "question": "৩৭) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_CXMOwq1.png\" width=\"691\" height=\"63\">", "option1": "&nbsp;Yes, everywhere", "option2": "Only at <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">z = 0</span></span>", "option3": "Only along <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">x = 0</span></span>", "option4": "Not analytic anywhere", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_UJfgXRi.png\" width=\"539\" height=\"149\"></p>"}, {"id": "38", "question": "৩৮) If f(z) = u(x, y) + iv(x, y) is analytic at a point, which of the following must hold?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_8vtOPt9.png\" width=\"227\" height=\"60\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_gdUpJKa.png\" width=\"217\" height=\"47\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_0EgMsxv.png\" width=\"278\" height=\"38\">", "option4": "None of the above", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip4_Yh7xyoM.png\" width=\"467\" height=\"124\"></p>"}, {"id": "39", "question": "৩৯) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_j5vznVe.png\" width=\"539\" height=\"72\">", "option1": "&nbsp;Differentiable only at&nbsp;<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\">z=0</span></span>", "option2": "Differentiable everywhere", "option3": "Not differentiable anywhere", "option4": "Entire", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_cymHTta.png\" width=\"475\" height=\"273\"></p>"}, {"id": "40", "question": "৪০) Which of the following functions is <strong data-start=\"1711\" data-end=\"1734\">analytic everywhere</strong> (entire)?", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_Nvy5yTu.png\" width=\"374\" height=\"56\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_vilMvu7.png\" width=\"241\" height=\"74\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_vAzGwcI.png\" width=\"197\" height=\"63\">", "option4": "All of these", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_PnP2Z56.png\" width=\"268\" height=\"53\"></p>"}]}, "_source": "archive-question-subject", "_exam_id": 12101, "custom_field": "প্রতি প্রশ্নের মান ১ ও ভুল উত্তরের জন্য ০.৫০ কাটা যাবে।", "exam_time": "2700000", "is_omr": true, "omr_time": "3000000", "examname": "Sep 05, 2025", "type": "Math-Sub-561-applied", "payment": "BALANCE_NOT"}